# =============================================================================
# .dockerignore — Frontend build exclusions
# =============================================================================
# Same concept as the backend .dockerignore: keep the build context small
# and avoid sending irrelevant files to the Docker daemon.
# =============================================================================

# Git directory — repo history and metadata is not needed in the container.
# This folder can be surprisingly large (every commit ever) and has no
# purpose inside a web server container.
.git/

# Markdown files — documentation like README.md is for developers reading
# the repo, not for the nginx container serving your web app.
*.md

# The .dockerignore file itself — a bit meta, but there's no reason to
# copy this file into the image. It's only used during the build process.
.dockerignore
